WEBVTT

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:11.140
With the rapid development of Hyper Technology came the Labor...

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:15.240
a multi-purpose, humanoid construction machine whose use...

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.150
spread into almost every field.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:23.190
However, this gave rise to a new threat to society: Labor crime.

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:31.170
The Tokyo Metro Police founded the Special Vehicles, Section 2...

00:00:31.270 --> 00:00:35.540
within the Security Division to combat these ever-growing crimes.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:41.580
This was the beginning of the SV2 Patrol Labor... Patlabor... units.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:01:03.080
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:09.560
HAATO BIITO wo awaserya sore de ikisou yo
If I can get my heartbeat under control, I think I'll make it

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:15.270
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:01:15.530 --> 00:01:20.910
takaku hayaku suki yo ki mama ni
Higher, faster, I'll love you if I want to

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:27.460
METARU BODII no hadazawari sae
I think I'll get to like

00:01:27.650 --> 00:01:33.400
atsuku kanjite kuru kuse ni narisou
The way I get flushed at the touch of your metal body

00:01:33.710 --> 00:01:39.690
CHACHI na Imagination koeta jigen de
Oh, don't stop this gravity-defying feeling

00:01:39.730 --> 00:01:46.580
juuryokuihan ah nukeru Feeling tomenai de
That goes way beyond mere imagination

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:53.100
kimi ni ikarete METAMETA MECHAMEKA gurui
You really threw a wrench into my works

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:59.550
PITAri kakarerya PIKAA kireru ARUFONSU
When I hold him tight, my Alphonse can do anything

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:05.180
kimi to atashi wa miraiha koi no TEKUNISHAN
We're futurists, you and me; technicians of love

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:13.760
sora mo umi mo kyou mo ashita mo Nothin' impossible
Anytime, anywhere, nothing's impossible

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:17.720
Nothing's impossible

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:00.480
SV2 maintenance here.

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:02.620
Chief!

00:03:03.650 --> 00:03:05.020
Chief!

00:03:05.560 --> 00:03:07.920
We just got a confirmation call from the manufacturer!

00:03:08.030 --> 00:03:12.990
Three Ingram AV-98 Patrol Labors, along with their transport trailers...

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.660
left their Hachiouji factory at 7 this morning!

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:18.170
Their ETA is 11:00 AM.

00:03:18.270 --> 00:03:19.390
Good.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:21.430
- Old Man.
- What?

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:24.900
The new Labors are finally coming!

00:03:25.010 --> 00:03:26.530
What about it?

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:31.950
I'm so happy I could cry!

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.710
We're supposed to be the Metro Police's high-tech vanguard squad...

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:36.450
the forerunners of the police of the future!

00:03:36.550 --> 00:03:39.520
But the truth is, with all the budgeting and planning problems...

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:42.320
we're stuck out here in this reclaimed area...

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:46.690
and our "equipment" is just three second-hand construction Labors...

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:48.660
that were painted black and white!

00:03:48.770 --> 00:03:51.000
In the three months since the SV2 was founded...

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:54.590
they've looked down on us, calling us the force's trash!

00:03:54.710 --> 00:03:56.730
Their <i>appendix!</i> A fifth wheel!

00:03:56.840 --> 00:04:01.240
It's been rough on the squad, especially us maintenance people!

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:05.440
But today, we'll kiss those hard days goodbye...

00:04:05.550 --> 00:04:07.610
with the arrival of those three new Labors...

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.710
as we're reborn as a <i>real</i> Patrol Labor unit, a proud unit...

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:14.260
that will drive a wedge of justice into the tumultuous days to come!

00:04:14.360 --> 00:04:15.660
Shige.

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:20.790
When I was 12, my dad beat me for taking apart...

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.200
our footwarmer-engine scooter.

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:28.600
In the fifty years since then, machines have been my life.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:31.870
I don't have any pretensions or vanity anymore.

00:04:32.210 --> 00:04:34.110
But...

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:40.120
I want to see those brand-new machines more than anyone;

00:04:40.220 --> 00:04:43.380
I want to fiddle with 'em, take 'em apart.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:47.790
I've been standing out here all morning with that on my mind.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:53.490
I'm a machine moron, an outdated nuts 'n bolts kind of guy.

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.200
A shuttle from headquarters?

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:04.400
I wonder what they're doing out here at this hour?

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:23.890
I've seen something like this in a movie.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:26.860
It was something like "Rabaul" or "Fighter Zero" or "One Family"...

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:28.520
with no women in them;

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:31.470
the mechanics were in the mafia, 'n were always drinking, gambling...

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:35.100
cooking rice in outdoor cookers, 'n bonding by fighting all the time.

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:37.230
So? That's the army.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.640
Cops and the army both have ranks and guns... what's the difference?

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:46.110
He has a point. It certainly doesn't seem like Tokyo out here.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:48.280
Now's the time to run.

00:05:48.390 --> 00:05:53.320
Run if you want. But if you do, I'll shoot you for desertion.

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:55.450
Now <i>that's</i> the army.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:05:58.820
Hey! You new guys out front!

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.020
Up here!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:04.030
Bring your papers with you and assemble in the SV2 Chief's Office!

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.260
Damn, he spotted us.

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.340
Let's go!

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:08.130
Move it!

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:10.330
Hello.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.710
Looks like your personnel got here first.

00:06:15.810 --> 00:06:17.640
I hope you have some worthwhile people.

00:06:17.750 --> 00:06:19.810
Why wouldn't I?

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:23.280
They passed up <i>my</i> unit of veterans and gave <i>you...</i>

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:27.650
those top-of-the-line Labors. You'd <i>better</i> have some good people.

00:06:27.790 --> 00:06:33.730
That was HQ's decision. The same with the five people they chose.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:35.660
Five?

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.500
I'm missing one.

00:06:42.210 --> 00:06:45.660
Hey! This area's off-limits to civilians!

00:06:45.780 --> 00:06:48.400
If you play around here, you're gonna get arrested.

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:54.680
Officer Noa Izumi reporting for duty with the Security Division's...

00:06:54.790 --> 00:06:57.810
Special Vehicles Section 2, Second Unit.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.780
Nice to meet you!

00:07:00.660 --> 00:07:02.320
All right, here are your assignments:

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:04.650
Unit 1: Forward, Noa Izumi.

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:05.820
Yes!

00:07:05.930 --> 00:07:07.790
Backup, Asuma Shinohara.

00:07:08.270 --> 00:07:10.790
Unit 2: Forward, Isao Ota.

00:07:10.900 --> 00:07:12.800
Backup, Mikiyasu Shinshi.

00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:15.970
Power Crew, Hiromi Yamazaki.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:20.140
I <i>had</i> planned to wait for the new Labors to get here...

00:07:20.240 --> 00:07:24.840
and then assign them immediately so you could start their patterning.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.310
Chief!

00:07:27.420 --> 00:07:29.780
But it looks like it's still going to be a while...

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.680
so why don't you go grab something to eat?

00:07:31.790 --> 00:07:32.850
Yes, sir!

00:07:33.720 --> 00:07:35.020
Chief!

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:38.850
It's an urgent call from the transport driver, Chief.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:43.060
Sakaki here.

00:07:48.140 --> 00:07:50.900
We're stuck in weekend traffic!

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:55.710
With those bombings in Shiba and Takebashi, we can't move an inch!

00:07:55.810 --> 00:07:58.980
We're right in front of the Miyakezaka interchange now.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:05.310
I didn't wanna use the expressway because it's a priority delivery.

00:08:05.420 --> 00:08:08.690
But with that Labor being hijacked on the highway just last week...

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:12.230
your chief told us to make sure we used the expressway.

00:08:12.330 --> 00:08:15.090
He said the police would never live it down...

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:17.600
if one of their own Labors got stolen.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:19.590
Huh? What?

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:21.330
QUIET!

00:08:22.040 --> 00:08:25.740
Um, it's nothing. I was talking to someone over here.

00:08:26.010 --> 00:08:28.980
Huh? You're going to wait until the Labors get there?

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:32.980
I don't mind, but I don't know when we're gonna get there.

00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:42.380
So he's been waiting out there since this morning.

00:08:42.930 --> 00:08:45.290
He can be pretty stubborn.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:48.990
He must really like Labors. I think we'll get along!

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:51.070
From what I've heard, he's been a mechanic...

00:08:51.170 --> 00:08:54.000
ever since they founded the motorcycle police corps.

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.630
When he goes down to HQ, they say...

00:08:55.740 --> 00:08:58.830
the Maintenance Division Chief himself greets him at the door.

00:08:58.940 --> 00:09:01.310
Heck, he's like God to us.

00:09:02.980 --> 00:09:04.140
Wow.

00:09:04.380 --> 00:09:06.110
No matter what it says on paper...

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:08.840
the top dog around here is Old Man Sakaki.

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:12.580
#2 is Captain Nagumo, the First Unit's chief.

00:09:12.760 --> 00:09:18.700
And I guess way down there in a distant third is your Captain Goto.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.200
Hey, what's the matter? Aren't you gonna eat any lunch?

00:09:25.300 --> 00:09:27.330
I didn't bring one.

00:09:31.170 --> 00:09:35.170
Man, I wish I had a girlfriend to make <i>my</i> lunch for me.

00:09:35.280 --> 00:09:39.040
I made this. Would you like one?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.820
Is there any place around here that delivers?

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:49.690
Heck, any place delivers if you order more than two items.

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.730
It'll take more than an hour, though.

00:09:52.360 --> 00:09:55.890
There's a corner store run by an old lady a couple of miles away.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.400
Want to borrow a bike? The handlebar's bent, though.

00:09:59.640 --> 00:10:04.870
Guns? You mean the Labors' 20mm revolver cannons?

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.400
Sure, we keep 'em in here, but you need the Old Man's okay to open it.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:14.780
You want me to let you use a 20mm because you want some practice?

00:10:14.890 --> 00:10:17.880
If you want to practice, go get permission from your captain.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.180
Shooting practice?

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:25.620
I ought to have experience with live ammo before I'm sent out.

00:10:25.730 --> 00:10:27.560
How are you going to fire it without a Labor?

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:30.290
- I'll borrow one from the First Unit!
- I doubt they'll lend you one.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:32.300
Then once my Labor gets here...

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:37.430
You can only fire a gun of that caliber at the Fuji shooting range...

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:40.700
and the Self Defense Forces have it booked through winter.

00:10:40.810 --> 00:10:46.040
What about shotguns? I've heard Labor Unit members can use them.

00:10:46.150 --> 00:10:47.580
Ota!

00:10:47.680 --> 00:10:50.980
You have to put in an application to get ammunition...

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:54.220
and it takes a month to get it after a strict review.

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:57.190
You can expect one shooting practice session a year, tops.

00:10:57.290 --> 00:11:01.160
Then how am I supposed to fulfill my duties when the time comes?

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.260
Come on, Ota, call it quits.

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:06.500
You'll have to. "Don't waste valuable bullets...

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:09.540
and avoid live-fire practice as much as possible.

00:11:09.640 --> 00:11:12.130
Should the need arise, do the job with one shot."

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:15.440
That's the way it is for soldiers and cops here in Japan.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:19.170
That doesn't make any sense! Let me... Let me fire a gun, sir!

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:20.750
Let me...

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.750
Let me shoot a gun, damn it!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.830
There's nobody here!

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:37.560
Does the First Unit have the day off?

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:38.630
Get real.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:40.640
There was an explosion on an expressway interchange...

00:11:40.740 --> 00:11:42.830
and they were sent out as backup a while ago.

00:11:44.570 --> 00:11:45.700
Found one!

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:50.970
So this is the first Patlabor model.

00:11:51.080 --> 00:11:53.110
Don't you think he looks like a bad guy, kinda?

00:11:53.580 --> 00:11:57.110
It's called the first, but it's basically just an Asuka 95...

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:59.580
civil engineering Labor that's been upgraded.

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.490
But the Type-98 AV Patrol Labor is a whole different beast.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:07.290
It was built for anti-Labor combat, and deliberately designed...

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:12.270
to have a psychological impact on anyone who sees it.

00:12:13.500 --> 00:12:14.770
You're a strange guy, Asuma-kun.

00:12:14.870 --> 00:12:17.170
For someone who doesn't know much about Labor units...

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:20.070
you sure seem to know a lot about Labors.

00:12:21.210 --> 00:12:23.910
Yeah, I guess.

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:28.150
Hey, Asuma-kun.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:31.550
- Stop calling me Asuma-<i>kun</i>, okay?
- Why?

00:12:31.650 --> 00:12:33.380
I don't like being called that by a woman.

00:12:33.490 --> 00:12:35.520
What should I call you, then?

00:12:35.630 --> 00:12:37.590
Figure it out yourself!

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:40.460
Geez, this guy sure acts high n' mighty.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.560
Asuma Shinohara... Shinohara...

00:12:43.670 --> 00:12:46.100
I know that name from someplace.

00:12:46.450 --> 00:12:49.450
Shinohara Heavy Industries

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.170
Hey, Otaku.

00:12:51.270 --> 00:12:53.140
Don't call me "Otaku"!

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.780
Are you related to someone at Shinohara Heavy Industries, Asuma?

00:12:57.880 --> 00:13:00.280
It's my dad's company.

00:13:01.480 --> 00:13:03.950
No kidding. I had a feeling...

00:13:04.890 --> 00:13:07.250
No way! It's your dad's company?

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:11.990
You're the son of the president of Shinohara Heavy Industries?

00:13:12.300 --> 00:13:16.130
What? How come his <i>son</i> is a public servant?

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:19.070
- Well?
- My parents suckered me into it.

00:13:19.170 --> 00:13:22.430
Oh, there you are! We've got work to do!

00:13:30.150 --> 00:13:33.640
Dad, you bastard. You go and sign me up on the sly...

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:36.580
and then use your connections to get me accepted.

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:39.350
"For my education," my butt.

00:13:39.460 --> 00:13:42.890
Sounds like he didn't have much faith in you as his successor.

00:13:42.990 --> 00:13:46.290
So what about <i>you?</i> What made you join up?

00:13:46.400 --> 00:13:49.990
Me? To pilot Alphonse, of course.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:52.960
"Alphonse"? What's that?

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:55.340
My Pattie's name!

00:13:55.440 --> 00:13:58.200
I've been working on it since I decided to join up!

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:03.140
Man, it must be nice to get a job that you actually <i>want</i> to do.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.940
Yeah, and I even got selected as a Forward!

00:14:06.820 --> 00:14:09.410
I don't know <i>what</i> I would've done if I got into the Labor unit...

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.880
but couldn't pilot a Labor.

00:14:11.150 --> 00:14:13.350
Shit! This sucks!

00:14:13.460 --> 00:14:17.390
Why am I being forced to cut grass out here at the ends of the earth?

00:14:17.490 --> 00:14:20.330
Let me shoot a gun, damn it!

00:14:20.530 --> 00:14:21.790
I'm gonna run away!

00:14:22.200 --> 00:14:24.560
Cut. And cut.

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:27.800
Cut. And cut.

00:14:28.130 --> 00:14:32.850
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:14:33.130 --> 00:14:37.850
<i>Patlabor</i>

00:15:08.970 --> 00:15:11.530
Uh, Tamiko? It's Mikiyasu.

00:15:11.640 --> 00:15:14.440
I know it's sudden, but we're on the night shift starting tonight.

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:15.630
I'm sorry.

00:15:15.740 --> 00:15:17.270
No, I've eaten.

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:20.770
Instant ramen and some melon-jam muffins.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:23.040
It was delicious.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:26.580
Because of these explosions, traffic on the Metro expressway...

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:29.590
is still at a standstill, and near the Takabashi interchange...

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:32.520
Akemi Ito, a housewife from Musashino, went into labor...

00:15:32.620 --> 00:15:34.390
This stinks.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:38.280
There's no telling <i>when</i> I'll finally get to meet Alphonse!

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:41.330
What were they thinking when they decided to go through a...

00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:44.490
perpetual parking lot like the Shuto Expressway, of all places?

00:15:44.600 --> 00:15:47.730
Thanks to them, just when I thought we were getting off with...

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:51.100
just a day of cutting grass, they stick us with night duty.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:54.640
If we had some beer here, maybe we could enjoy it...

00:15:54.750 --> 00:15:59.120
but all we have is oolong tea and some nuts. This is pathetic.

00:16:01.050 --> 00:16:02.020
This stinks.

00:16:02.420 --> 00:16:06.920
Watch it, slacker! You're on duty!

00:16:07.090 --> 00:16:09.650
C'mon, nothing's gonna happen on our first day.

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:13.060
And even if something <i>did,</i> what can we do without any Labors?

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.330
Hey! Shinohara!

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.420
<i>Now</i> what?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:17.730
Turn that up.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.000
Report from 8th Precinct:

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:26.700
Unidentified Labor spotted near the mouth of the Sumida River.

00:16:26.810 --> 00:16:29.540
It escaped from the Maritime Police and is moving up the river.

00:16:29.650 --> 00:16:31.710
It is currently moving northward.

00:16:31.820 --> 00:16:35.550
It is armed with an unidentified weapon. Use extreme caution.

00:16:35.650 --> 00:16:37.280
Report from 8th Precinct:

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:41.760
Unidentified Labor spotted near the mouth of the Sumida River.

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.390
Come on, Shinshi! Hurry! We're meeting in the hangar!

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.550
Coming!

00:16:50.200 --> 00:16:53.870
Dispatch orders for the Second Unit have just come down.

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:56.370
We're not sure what we're up against, but it's...

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:00.410
a powerhouse that took out a Maritime Agency boat with one shot.

00:17:00.510 --> 00:17:06.040
As you all know, our Labors are still stuck near Edobashi.

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:08.450
With that in mind...

00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:11.950
we're going to go pick them up.

00:17:12.360 --> 00:17:15.620
Yamazaki will borrow the First Unit's #3 trailer and leave...

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.920
immediately for Edobashi with Izumi and Ota.

00:17:19.360 --> 00:17:22.930
Izumi and Ota will then activate Labors 1 and 2.

00:17:23.040 --> 00:17:26.370
They will then meet with Shinohara and Shinshi, who will go on ahead...

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:28.960
in their command cars, and run their initial pattern loads.

00:17:29.510 --> 00:17:34.470
I'll contact you via radio as to where to meet and how to proceed.

00:17:34.580 --> 00:17:36.670
Don't waste any time.

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:37.910
That's all.

00:17:38.120 --> 00:17:39.080
Any questions?

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:41.680
- Yeah!
- Right here!

00:17:50.930 --> 00:17:54.700
I'm sorry for calling so late. My name is Goto, I'm with the SV2.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.460
May I speak to your daughter Shinobu, please?

00:18:06.280 --> 00:18:09.410
Systems E, F, G, L, M activated.

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:10.710
Unit 1, activated!

00:18:10.980 --> 00:18:14.440
System C synchronized! Systems G, H, J, L, M activated.

00:18:14.550 --> 00:18:16.580
Unit 2, activated! Raise me!

00:18:16.790 --> 00:18:20.160
You sure? If anything happens, it ain't gonna be on <i>my</i> head!

00:18:20.260 --> 00:18:21.590
Can it! Just do it!

00:18:21.690 --> 00:18:22.820
You got it!

00:18:59.330 --> 00:19:03.460
Excuse me. Pardon me. Sorry.

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:10.470
Ota! Jump! Jump!

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:13.310
Hello?

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:16.680
What do you mean, "Hello?" How's it coming?

00:19:16.780 --> 00:19:20.980
Both units have been activated. Now beginning retriev...

00:19:24.220 --> 00:19:25.660
To all cars on patrol.

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:28.350
Target came ashore at the Asakusa-Azumabashi...

00:19:28.460 --> 00:19:29.980
and is now heading for Kokusai Avenue.

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:32.690
Target ID'd as a Shinohara Type-98 "Pickle"...

00:19:32.800 --> 00:19:34.660
mountain construction Labor.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.270
Target's original intent believed to be terrorist activities in...

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:39.670
the New South Senjuu midtown area, but details are unclear.

00:19:41.370 --> 00:19:44.340
Shinshi, you take Uguisudani. Shinohara, take Joumyou Temple.

00:19:44.440 --> 00:19:45.530
Set up a dragnet.

00:19:45.640 --> 00:19:49.170
Guide our guest off of Kototoi Avenue into Ueno Park.

00:19:49.680 --> 00:19:53.450
Wouldn't it be better to take it on near Iriya, Captain?

00:19:53.550 --> 00:19:55.380
- No.
- Why not?

00:19:55.590 --> 00:19:58.890
That's where I was born.

00:19:59.960 --> 00:20:02.590
Have you finished the retrieval, Yamazaki?

00:20:02.690 --> 00:20:03.850
Do you read me? Over.

00:20:04.230 --> 00:20:08.290
Unit 2 has been retrieved, but Unit 1 is, uh...

00:20:08.400 --> 00:20:11.860
What's wrong with Unit 1? What're you doing over there, Izumi?

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:16.840
No way! If I jump from here, I'll bust Alphonse!

00:20:35.890 --> 00:20:38.690
Target now turning off of Kokusai Avenue onto Kototoi Avenue.

00:20:38.800 --> 00:20:42.030
Target now turning off of Kokusai Avenue onto Kototoi Ave.

00:20:46.670 --> 00:20:49.470
The Iriya intersection and Showa Avenue roadblocks are ready!

00:20:49.570 --> 00:20:52.040
B Squad, back up C Squad! Guard the entrance to Ueno Park!

00:20:52.140 --> 00:20:55.080
Almost all the civilians have been evacuated from the park!

00:20:55.180 --> 00:20:57.110
Okay, good work.

00:21:03.020 --> 00:21:06.220
"March, the month of Spring. Strangled and left behind, the dead...

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.520
dances in the flowers."

00:21:09.730 --> 00:21:11.530
Oh, what the hell.

00:21:18.640 --> 00:21:21.540
Looks like the gang's all here.

00:21:21.840 --> 00:21:24.100
Okay, it's time to get to work.

00:21:25.680 --> 00:21:27.840
All units, report in.

00:21:27.950 --> 00:21:30.810
Uguisudani here. Unit 2 in position.

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:31.880
Joumyou Temple here.

00:21:32.280 --> 00:21:35.250
Initial pattern load complete. Now in position.

00:21:35.350 --> 00:21:37.880
Okay, looks like we managed to squeak by.

00:21:41.260 --> 00:21:44.020
Don't worry. You both have Shinohara Labors...

00:21:44.130 --> 00:21:45.960
but we have the advantage, specs-wise.

00:21:46.060 --> 00:21:49.030
"Pickle." What a dumb name.

00:21:49.130 --> 00:21:50.800
That's what <i>I</i> thought.

00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:04.580
You want some? Come and get it, criminal!

00:22:04.980 --> 00:22:09.350
You won't get one step past me!

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:12.420
What're you talking about? He's <i>supposed</i> to get past us!

00:22:12.520 --> 00:22:15.360
Our job is to keep it from going north towards Nippori...

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:17.090
and guide it towards Ueno Park!

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:18.560
Shut up!

00:22:18.660 --> 00:22:22.930
If I pump it full of lead right here, that'll be the end of it!

00:22:23.030 --> 00:22:24.020
Here it comes!

00:22:24.140 --> 00:22:26.230
Distance, 300... 250...

00:22:26.340 --> 00:22:27.930
200... 150...

00:22:28.140 --> 00:22:30.160
You just bought it!

00:22:42.220 --> 00:22:44.590
H-His head! His head!

00:22:52.000 --> 00:22:54.060
Ota! Ota!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.430
The squad cars are wiped out? It knocked Ota's <i>head</i> off?

00:22:59.540 --> 00:23:00.770
No!

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.330
That damned homicidal Labor.

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:07.110
Noa! That guy's a moron, but he's been your partner for a day!

00:23:07.210 --> 00:23:08.300
Get even for him!

00:23:08.610 --> 00:23:11.880
No way! I don't wanna take that thing on!

00:23:11.980 --> 00:23:12.950
Stop babbling!

00:23:18.390 --> 00:23:20.980
Stay away! Don't come this way!

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.360
Go away!

00:23:42.980 --> 00:23:44.180
Noa! Go left!

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:55.950
This is Unit 1! Target is fleeing towards Ueno Park as planned!

00:23:56.060 --> 00:23:57.550
Now in pursuit!

00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:00.000
Noa! Hey, Noa! What're you doing?

00:24:04.770 --> 00:24:09.570
Alphonse. Alphonse got turned into the One-Armed Man!

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:12.410
This is no time to cry! Go after him! Fight, Noa!

00:24:12.510 --> 00:24:15.910
Turn that grief into rage and nail that three-legged bastard...

00:24:16.010 --> 00:24:17.640
with the Fist of Justice!

00:24:18.720 --> 00:24:20.380
That son of a...

00:24:20.490 --> 00:24:22.080
That son of a bitch!

00:24:51.250 --> 00:24:54.310
Man, I can't believe we ran out of gas.

00:24:54.420 --> 00:24:57.120
This area's crawling with cops. Let's get out of here!

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.250
You are completely surrounded!

00:25:01.360 --> 00:25:03.920
Throw down your weapons and exit the Labor immediately!

00:25:04.130 --> 00:25:06.260
You are completely surrounded!

00:25:06.360 --> 00:25:09.330
Throw down your weapons and exit the Labor immediately!

00:25:13.300 --> 00:25:14.600
He's bluffing.

00:25:14.910 --> 00:25:17.530
Listen up! This ain't one of the toys we've been using!

00:25:17.640 --> 00:25:19.610
This is a real anti-tank missile!

00:25:19.710 --> 00:25:23.510
If you move even an inch, I'll fire it into that museum!

00:25:23.820 --> 00:25:27.510
<i>This</i> is why I didn't want to lead them in here!

00:25:27.620 --> 00:25:29.020
He's bluffing, I'm telling you.

00:25:29.350 --> 00:25:33.790
Okay! I want a getaway car here inside of five minutes...

00:25:33.890 --> 00:25:36.620
along with food and a million bucks in old 10-dollar bills!

00:25:36.730 --> 00:25:38.530
<i>There</i> you are!

00:25:39.460 --> 00:25:41.430
Hold it right there!

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:44.830
Freeze! If you don't, I'll...

00:25:45.000 --> 00:25:47.630
Shut up! Taste the Fist of Justice!

00:25:47.740 --> 00:25:49.670
Rocket Punch!

00:26:07.930 --> 00:26:11.450
Just when I thought I couldn't wait any more...

00:26:11.560 --> 00:26:14.590
I get one with no head and another with one arm.

00:26:15.700 --> 00:26:17.930
You can fix them... right?

00:26:18.040 --> 00:26:19.660
I can fix them.

00:26:21.370 --> 00:26:22.960
Please take good care of them!

00:26:23.070 --> 00:26:24.840
- Shige! Get me cutting pliers!
- Yes, sir!

00:26:26.780 --> 00:26:27.870
Hey.

00:26:27.980 --> 00:26:30.310
I thought you said I had the advantage, spec-wise.

00:26:30.420 --> 00:26:31.780
Did I say that?

00:26:31.880 --> 00:26:33.180
Yeah.

00:26:33.280 --> 00:26:36.050
Well, it must've been that... what do you call it... <i>arms</i> gap.

00:26:36.150 --> 00:26:38.550
I beat a three-armed Labor with just <i>one.</i>

00:26:38.660 --> 00:26:40.590
Huh? Weren't those <i>legs?</i>

00:26:51.070 --> 00:26:55.170
I'm sorry I called you in, but we couldn't have done it without you.

00:26:55.270 --> 00:26:58.570
I don't let my personal feelings interfere with my work.

00:26:58.680 --> 00:27:03.310
I still think that HQ screwed up somewhere along the line.

00:27:03.410 --> 00:27:06.010
It would've been far more effective...

00:27:06.120 --> 00:27:09.640
if they'd have given those new Labors to <i>my</i> unit.

00:27:12.760 --> 00:27:13.990
You want them?

00:27:15.260 --> 00:27:18.060
The new Labors, I mean.

00:27:20.470 --> 00:27:21.560
I want them.

00:27:24.670 --> 00:27:26.160
You can't have them.

00:27:43.680 --> 00:27:48.680
Second Unit, Move Out <i>!</i>

00:28:47.750 --> 00:28:50.350
Wrapped in an air of danger, a woman comes to the base.

00:28:50.460 --> 00:28:52.510
What's the information that she brings to Tokyo...

00:28:52.620 --> 00:28:55.350
which is on full alert before the mayor of New York comes to Japan?

00:28:55.460 --> 00:28:56.950
I feel sorry for you, Asuma!

00:28:57.060 --> 00:28:58.620
Next time! "Long Shot"!

00:28:58.730 --> 00:29:01.060
Target, lock on!
